    fix(harness): tolerate string-contaminated columns in cell summary
    
    A pkill -9 during an append-only CSV write leaves a truncated final row.
    On resume the harness reloads that CSV (real_trace_experiments.py:1240),
    the bad row makes a numeric column object-dtype, and build_pilot_summary's
    .mean() does str+float -> the whole cell crashes AFTER completing hours of
    collection (yi x math died after 5h this way). Add _safe_mean (coerce to
    numeric, NaN out the junk) at every summary mean so one truncated row can
    never nuke a cell again. Belt-and-suspenders for the upcoming ARC/GPQA cells.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

